### Pick 5 — The Milgrain Vintage Rose Gold (Best Romantic)

**Milgrain Lace Pavé Vintage-Style Engagement Ring in 14K Rose Gold by James Allen**

- Setting price: [$2,650](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/milgrain-lace-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315056?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- Stone: [0.75ct D VVS1 Excellent IGI Marquise Lab](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29945507?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — $643
- **Total ring: $3,293**

[![Milgrain Lace Pavé Rose Gold Vintage Style Marquise Engagement Ring with 0.75ct D VVS1 lab diamond](/images/vintage-marquise-diamond-ring-white-gold-milgrain-detail.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/milgrain-lace-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315056?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

Milgrain is the row of tiny beads along the edge of a setting. It came from Art Deco and Edwardian jewelry. On a rose gold band, it creates a warmth that no plain-shank setting achieves. The lace-style pavé adds a delicate texture to the shoulders.

A marquise stone in a vintage-inspired rose gold setting is a high-contrast combination. The elongated, geometric marquise against the curved milgrain detailing creates tension. That tension is the appeal — it looks like an heirloom, not a mass-produced ring.

The 0.75ct D VVS1 lab at $643 is the right size for this head. A 1ct stone would overwhelm the delicate milgrain detail. The 0.75ct lets the setting breathe.

**Who this is for:** You want a ring with personality. You love rose gold and vintage aesthetics. You don't want something that looks like every other engagement ring.

