[![Marquise Cut Side Stone Yellow Gold Natural GIA Engagement Ring with 0.75ct G VS1 diamond](/images/yellow-gold-marquise-engagement-ring-top-view.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-side-stone-diamond-shared-prong-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-305148?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

This is the natural stone pick. A GIA-certified 0.75ct G VS1 marquise, formed over billions of years, set in a marquise-specific side stone head. The setting was designed for marquise stones. The shared-prong shoulder diamonds mirror the elongated profile of the center.

G color in yellow gold is a classic pairing. The slight warmth of G color in white metal can look off-color. In yellow gold, it disappears. The gold absorbs the color. You get a bright, face-up white stone in a warm metal with a clear resale pedigree.

The GIA certificate on this stone adds $300–$600 to its secondary market value compared to an uncertified natural. If you ever sell or trade up, GIA documentation matters. See the full explanation in our [GIA certified marquise diamond guide](/gia-certified-marquise-diamond).

**Who this is for:** You want natural. You care about long-term value. You want yellow gold and a setting built for marquise stones specifically.

