[![Floral Marquise Diamond Engagement Ring 18K White Gold with 0.75ct H VS1 natural GIA diamond](/images/marquise-halo-engagement-ring-white-gold-platinum.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/floral-marquise-diamond-engagement-ring-in-18k-white-gold-item-203738?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

18K gold is denser than 14K — 75% pure gold vs 58.5%. The color is richer, the weight is noticeable, and the prestige is higher. This setting has a floral motif around the head — a nod to antique and Art Nouveau design. It's built for marquise stones specifically.

The GIA-certified 0.75ct H VS1 Ideal cut marquise is a sweet-spot natural stone. H color is near-colorless and works beautifully in white metal. VS1 clarity is eye-clean from every angle. The Ideal cut grade means this stone is optimized for brilliance.

This is not just a ring — it's a statement. The floral head, the 18K white gold, the GIA Ideal cut center. For $4,172, you get a ring that looks like it belongs in a boutique at twice the price.

**Who this is for:** You want a natural stone with visible craftsmanship in the setting. You notice the difference between 14K and 18K. You want a ring that stands out in a room.

